Retain the CIX display fixes that are safe for production: ACPI/OF
enumeration, firmware-node lifetime, optional panel resources, eDP power
rollback, fixed-clock builds and useful diagnostic severity.  Duplicate
configuration prompts and changes already supplied by earlier 7.2 patches
are omitted.

The Linux 7.2 port uses the refcounted DRM panel allocator and tightens the
ACPI pipeline parser so that owned firmware-node and clock references are
balanced.  It also propagates AVI infoframe packing failures instead of
discarding a negative result through an unsigned length.

This artifact is mechanically generated from the exact Linux 7.2.0 CIX
preimage immediately after patch 70120.

